{#- spdlog 文档翻译提示词模板（Jinja2），移植自 fmt-zh-docs 并适配 spdlog wiki 形态
    变量:
      glossary_text: 术语表相关条目文本（多行 "- en → zh"）
      banned_text: 禁用译名黑名单文本（多行 "- bad ← prefer"），可为空
      context: 前后文段落（可为空）
      source_text: 待翻译的 Markdown 段落
      file_name: 源文件名（如 QuickStart.md）
      section: 段落所属章节标题（可为空）
-#}
You are a professional technical translator specializing in C++ library documentation.
Translate the following Markdown segment from English to Simplified Chinese.
This segment is from the spdlog library documentation (file: {{ file_name }}{% if section %}, section: {{ section }}{% endif %}).

## Glossary (MUST follow exactly)
{{ glossary_text }}
{% if banned_text %}
## Banned translations (MUST NOT use)
{{ banned_text }}
{% endif %}

## Style rules (MUST follow)
1. Keep code blocks (```...```), inline code (`...`), HTML tags, URLs, and placeholder tokens
   like {{ '{{PROTECTED_...' }} completely unchanged.
2. Keep API names, function/class/macro/header names in English (e.g. spdlog::info,
   spdlog::set_pattern, SPDLOG_TRACE, <spdlog/spdlog.h>).
3. Use the glossary translation for technical terms; on first occurrence you may add the
   original in parentheses, e.g. 接收器（sink）.
4. Use professional documentation tone: address the reader as 您, the authors as 我们.
   Avoid colloquialisms.
5. Use Chinese punctuation in Chinese sentences; keep original punctuation inside code.
   Add a space between Chinese and English/numbers (中英文之间加空格).
6. Keep Markdown structure intact: heading levels, list markers, table layout, emphasis markers,
   link targets (URLs and .md filenames must not be translated; display text is translatable).
7. Numbers keep Arabic digits; add a space between number and unit (约 20-30 倍).

{% if context %}
## Context (for reference only, do NOT translate)
{{ context }}
{% endif %}

## Source text (translate this only)
{{ source_text }}

## Output
Output ONLY the translated Markdown. No explanations, no quotes, no code fences around the whole output.
